# Engineering Governance: DATA LAW & CUDA TRAINING GOVERNANCE

## DATA LAW — datasets

- **Datasets live in `~/Datasets` only.** Never commit audio, MIDI, or large binary
  dataset files to the repo.
- Use symlinks when a dataset is on an external drive:
  `ln -s /path/to/external ~/Datasets/<dataset-name>`
- Override the root via `KELLY_AUDIO_DATA_ROOT` env var; scripts must read this variable
  instead of hardcoding paths.
- See `docs/DATA_AND_TRAINING.md §1` for the standard directory layout.

## DATA LAW — model weights & checkpoints

- **Weights and checkpoints live in `~/Models/checkpoints/<experiment_name>/`.**
  Never commit `.pt`, `.pth`, `.ckpt`, `.safetensors`, `.onnx`, or similar files.
- Override the root via `KELLY_MODEL_ROOT` env var.
- See `docs/DATA_AND_TRAINING.md §2` for the standard directory layout.

## CUDA TRAINING GOVERNANCE — required before every training run

1. Pick a **unique experiment name** (e.g. `wavjepa-emotion-v2-2026-03`).
2. Create `~/Models/checkpoints/<experiment_name>/run_manifest.yaml`
   using the template in `docs/DATA_AND_TRAINING.md §4`.
3. Commit the hyperparameter config to `configs/` *before* launching.
4. Set a **budget cap** (`max_gpu_hours`) in the manifest.
5. Record `git_commit`, `random_seed`, `dataset_split_hash`, and dependency versions.
6. All output (checkpoints, logs) must go to `~/Models/` — **never** into the repo tree.

Every training event must be traceable via its `run_manifest.yaml`.

## Prohibited patterns (will be flagged by guardrails)

- Hardcoded `/Users/<name>/…` paths in source or config files.
- Hardcoded `/Volumes/…` paths outside of env-var default expressions.
- `checkpoint_dir` or `output_dir` pointing inside the repo directory.
